<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 22 June, from 168 BCE to 1944.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">168 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rome defeats Macedon at Pydna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lucius Aemilius Paullus's legions broke the Macedonian phalanx of King Perseus. The Antigonid kingdom was abolished, and Rome became the dominant power in the Greek world.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1633</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo is made to abjure before the Inquisition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Found 'vehemently suspect of heresy', Galileo formally abjured the view that the Earth moves around the Sun. He spent the rest of his life under house arrest.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1772</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lord Mansfield rules in the Somerset case</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The judge held that James Somerset, an enslaved man brought to England, could not be forcibly removed abroad. The ruling was widely taken to mean slavery had no basis in English law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1941</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades the Soviet Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Barbarossa sent some three million Axis troops across a front from the Baltic to the Black Sea. The war in the east became the largest and deadliest land conflict in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1944</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt signs the G.I. Bill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Servicemen's Readjustment Act gave veterans college tuition, low-cost home loans and unemployment pay. Millions took up its benefits, expanding higher education and home ownership.</p></li></ol>
